.TH CONDUCTOR 8 "2026-10-03" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor \- web administrator and self-service portal for Samba AD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor
serves the Samba Conductor web interface: administration of a Samba Active
Directory domain (users, groups, OUs, computers, DNS, Group Policy links,
password policies, lockouts, bulk operations) and a self-service portal.
Every directory operation uses the signed-in user's own Kerberos identity;
writes are previewed, confirmed and recorded in a hash-chained audit log.
Privileged local operations go through
.BR conductor-helper (8).
.PP
Each command accepts
.B \-h
for its flags.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the web server (normally started by
.BR conductor.service ).
.TP
.B setup
First-run configuration, as root: pins the domain CA, resolves the role
groups to SIDs, generates the TOTP key and writes
.IR /etc/conductor/conductor.toml .
.TP
.B enroll-link
Issue a one-time second-factor enrollment link, as the conductor user.
.TP
.B audit verify
Check the audit log hash chain, as the conductor user.
.TP
.B audit export
Write the audit log as JSON lines.
.TP
.B healthcheck
Exit 0 when the web listener answers a TLS handshake with conductor's own
certificate and, when enabled, the 2FA socket for conductor-idp exists
(container healthchecks).
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conductor/conductor.toml
Configuration, written by
.BR "conductor setup" .
.TP
.I /etc/conductor/credentials/totp-key
Key that seals the TOTP secrets, passed to the service as a systemd
credential. Keep an offline copy.
.TP
.I /etc/conductor/tls/
Web certificate and key.
.TP
.I /var/lib/conductor/conductor.db
State: sessions, settings, second factors, audit log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor-helper (8),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.I /usr/share/doc/conductor/README.Debian
